<title>PAKISTAN: PAKISTAN JULY CONSUMER PRICES AT 11.59 PCT YR/YR.</title>
<headline>PAKISTAN JULY CONSUMER PRICES AT 11.59 PCT YR/YR.</headline>
<dateline>ISLAMABAD 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's consumer price index rose 11.59 percent in July year-on-year compared with 12.45 percent in June and 10.32 in July 1996, the Federal Bureau of Statistics said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>The index, using 1990/91 as base year, rose by 0.62 percent in July to 198.17 from 196.95 in June. The index stood at 177.59 in July 1996.</p>
<p>					  July     June    July 1996</p>
<p>CONSUMER PRICE base 1990/91    198.17   196.95   177.59</p>
<p>    Month-on-month		   0.62   -0.31     +1.40</p>
<p>    Year-on-year		   +11.59   +12.45   +10.32</p>
<p>-- Islamabad Newsroom  (9251) 274757; Fax 274759</p>
